Subject: [PATCH] crypto: af_alg: add skcipher keystream-only operation
Upstream-Status: Pending

Add an explicit keystream-only operation for skcipher algorithms.

Userspace selects ALG_OP_KEYSTREAM_ONLY and supplies only an IV. recv()
then uses the size of the destination buffer as the requested keystream
length, without requiring a TX buffer filled with zeroes.

The kernel skcipher API exposes an optional generate_keystream callback.
Algorithms which do not implement it return -EOPNOTSUPP.

Implement the callback for ctr-aes-ingenic. The implementation reuses the
existing counter generation, DMA ping-pong, and IRQ chaining added by the
CTR fast-path patch, but copies raw AES-ECB(counter) output directly to the
destination instead of XORing it with source data.

Keystream-only requests must be a multiple of the algorithm chunksize.
For CTR-AES this is 16 bytes, avoiding implicit loss of a partial counter
block between requests.

diff --git a/include/uapi/linux/if_alg.h b/include/uapi/linux/if_alg.h
--- a/include/uapi/linux/if_alg.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/if_alg.h
@@ -57,6 +57,7 @@
 /* Operations */
 #define ALG_OP_DECRYPT			0
 #define ALG_OP_ENCRYPT			1
+#define ALG_OP_KEYSTREAM_ONLY		2

 #endif	/* _LINUX_IF_ALG_H */

